{
  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "a1",
      "type": "product",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/0",
      "span": {
        "offset": 0,
        "length": 37
      },
      "text": "PRODUCT REQUIREMENTS . INTERNAL TOOLS"
    },
    {
      "id": "a2",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/2",
      "span": {
        "offset": 51,
        "length": 99
      },
      "text": "One screen where a consultant tells us what they are good at - and it sticks the moment they click."
    },
    {
      "id": "a3",
      "type": "business-goal",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/4",
      "span": {
        "offset": 163,
        "length": 57
      },
      "text": "We cannot answer \"who knows Jira?\" without asking people."
    },
    {
      "id": "a4",
      "type": "integration",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/5",
      "span": {
        "offset": 307,
        "length": 45
      },
      "text": "Today that data lives in a Power Apps screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "a5",
      "type": "imposed-technology",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/6",
      "span": {
        "offset": 854,
        "length": 50
      },
      "text": "We are rebuilding it as a small Next.js/React app."
    },
    {
      "id": "a6",
      "type": "ux-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/8",
      "span": {
        "offset": 1066,
        "length": 163
      },
      "text": "A consultant can open the app, find the competency they have in mind, and record their level without thinking about the mechanics - no save step, no second screen."
    },
    {
      "id": "a7",
      "type": "non-functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/9",
      "span": {
        "offset": 1241,
        "length": 37
      },
      "text": "Nothing is ever lost to a closed tab.",
      "category": "REL"
    },
    {
      "id": "a8",
      "type": "ux-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/11",
      "span": {
        "offset": 1561,
        "length": 127
      },
      "text": "The words on the screen match the words the business uses, so nobody has to translate practitioner into advanced in their head."
    },
    {
      "id": "a9",
      "type": "user-class",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/13",
      "span": {
        "offset": 1705,
        "length": 64
      },
      "text": "One audience, and only one: the consultant assessing themselves."
    },
    {
      "id": "a10",
      "type": "out-of-scope",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/14",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2072,
        "length": 63
      },
      "text": "Managers, reviewers and staffing are not users of this release."
    },
    {
      "id": "a11",
      "type": "feature",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/17",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2296,
        "length": 55
      },
      "text": "Browsing the competency catalogue and narrowing it down"
    },
    {
      "id": "a12",
      "type": "feature",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/18",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2365,
        "length": 47
      },
      "text": "Recording, changing and clearing your own level"
    },
    {
      "id": "a13",
      "type": "integration",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/19",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2415,
        "length": 29
      },
      "text": "Signing in with corporate SSO"
    },
    {
      "id": "a14",
      "type": "out-of-scope",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/21",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2478,
        "length": 37
      },
      "text": "Manager, reviewer or validation views"
    },
    {
      "id": "a15",
      "type": "out-of-scope",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/23",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2572,
        "length": 36
      },
      "text": "Any way to edit the catalogue itself"
    },
    {
      "id": "a16",
      "type": "out-of-scope",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/25",
      "span": {
        "offset": 2707,
        "length": 34
      },
      "text": "Cross-employee search or reporting"
    },
    {
      "id": "a17",
      "type": "mockup",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/76",
      "span": {
        "offset": 3679,
        "length": 173
      },
      "text": "The shape of the thing is right and we are keeping it: one flat grid, one row per competency, showing its Type, its Area and its name, with three tick columns for the level."
    },
    {
      "id": "a18",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/87",
      "span": {
        "offset": 5106,
        "length": 143
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to drill into one family of competencies, so I am not scrolling past a thousand rows to reach the ten that describe me."
    },
    {
      "id": "a19",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/88",
      "span": {
        "offset": 5250,
        "length": 95
      },
      "text": "Picking a Type narrows the Area dropdown to that Type's Areas and the grid to that Type's rows."
    },
    {
      "id": "a20",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/92",
      "span": {
        "offset": 5620,
        "length": 107
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to type the name of the thing I know, because that is faster than navigating to it."
    },
    {
      "id": "a21",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/93",
      "span": {
        "offset": 5728,
        "length": 123
      },
      "text": "Typing in the competency box leaves only the rows whose competency name contains what was typed, ignoring case and accents."
    },
    {
      "id": "a22",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/97",
      "span": {
        "offset": 6056,
        "length": 139
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to review what I have already claimed, because correcting an old profile is a different job from filling a new one."
    },
    {
      "id": "a23",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/98",
      "span": {
        "offset": 6196,
        "length": 95
      },
      "text": "With Mine switched on, the grid shows only competencies where this person has a level recorded."
    },
    {
      "id": "a24",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/102",
      "span": {
        "offset": 6486,
        "length": 135
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to see only what is new since I was last here, so a two-month gap does not mean re-reading the whole catalogue."
    },
    {
      "id": "a25",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/103",
      "span": {
        "offset": 6622,
        "length": 152
      },
      "text": "With New switched on, the grid shows only competencies that were added to the catalogue after the last time this person changed any of their own levels."
    },
    {
      "id": "a26",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/109",
      "span": {
        "offset": 7540,
        "length": 128
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want one level per competency, because \"I am a Learner and an Expert at Jira\" is not a thing a person can be."
    },
    {
      "id": "a27",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/110",
      "span": {
        "offset": 7669,
        "length": 170
      },
      "text": "Ticking a level on a row that already holds a different one records the new level and clears the old, leaving exactly one of Learner, Advanced, Expert ticked on that row."
    },
    {
      "id": "a28",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/114",
      "span": {
        "offset": 8097,
        "length": 115
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to take a claim back, because a mis-click should not become a permanent statement about me."
    },
    {
      "id": "a29",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/115",
      "span": {
        "offset": 8213,
        "length": 149
      },
      "text": "Unticking the level a row currently holds deletes the claim outright and returns the row to unrated - which is a real state, distinct from \"Learner\"."
    },
    {
      "id": "a30",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/119",
      "span": {
        "offset": 8513,
        "length": 100
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want my click to be the whole interaction, so I never lose work by closing a tab."
    },
    {
      "id": "a31",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/120",
      "span": {
        "offset": 8614,
        "length": 84
      },
      "text": "Every level change is written as it happens, with no further action from the person."
    },
    {
      "id": "a32",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/124",
      "span": {
        "offset": 8930,
        "length": 137
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to be told when a click did not land, because silence would let me believe something false was recorded about me."
    },
    {
      "id": "a33",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/125",
      "span": {
        "offset": 9068,
        "length": 150
      },
      "text": "If a level change fails to write, the row goes back to its last saved level and a non-blocking message names the competency and says it was not saved."
    },
    {
      "id": "a34",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/130",
      "span": {
        "offset": 9540,
        "length": 119
      },
      "text": "As a consultant, I want to just be signed in, because this is an internal tool and I already have a corporate identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "a35",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/131",
      "span": {
        "offset": 9660,
        "length": 159
      },
      "text": "Opening any page unauthenticated sends the person to Microsoft Entra ID and brings them back to the page they asked for, signed in as their directory identity."
    },
    {
      "id": "a36",
      "type": "integration",
      "elementId": "figures/0",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10389,
        "length": 18
      },
      "text": "Microsoft Entra ID"
    },
    {
      "id": "a37",
      "type": "integration",
      "elementId": "figures/0",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10456,
        "length": 19
      },
      "text": "Power Apps \"Skills\""
    },
    {
      "id": "a38",
      "type": "imposed-technology",
      "elementId": "figures/0",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10338,
        "length": 10
      },
      "text": "PostgreSQL"
    },
    {
      "id": "a39",
      "type": "operational-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/147",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10548,
        "length": 181
      },
      "text": "The app stands alone. It owns its own PostgreSQL database and has exactly one live dependency - Microsoft Entra ID, for sign- in over OIDC with the authorization-code flow and PKCE."
    },
    {
      "id": "a40",
      "type": "data-entity",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/0",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10910,
        "length": 38
      },
      "text": "The catalogue Type - Area - Competency"
    },
    {
      "id": "a41",
      "type": "integration",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/1",
      "span": {
        "offset": 10949,
        "length": 65
      },
      "text": "Read-only to this app - it is maintained elsewhere and loaded in."
    },
    {
      "id": "a42",
      "type": "data-entity",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/2",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11126,
        "length": 10
      },
      "text": "The person"
    },
    {
      "id": "a43",
      "type": "data-requirement",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/3",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11137,
        "length": 90
      },
      "text": "A directory identity, keyed on their Entra object id, created the first time they sign in."
    },
    {
      "id": "a44",
      "type": "data-requirement",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/3",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11340,
        "length": 53
      },
      "text": "it has to survive them clearing every level they hold"
    },
    {
      "id": "a45",
      "type": "data-requirement",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/5",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11466,
        "length": 67
      },
      "text": "One person, one competency, one level: Learner, Advanced or Expert."
    },
    {
      "id": "a46",
      "type": "data-requirement",
      "elementId": "tables/2/cells/5",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11734,
        "length": 99
      },
      "text": "we keep it until twelve months after the person's account is disabled, and it never goes into logs."
    },
    {
      "id": "a47",
      "type": "assumption",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/156",
      "span": {
        "offset": 11860,
        "length": 54
      },
      "text": "The catalogue keeps being maintained outside this app."
    },
    {
      "id": "a48",
      "type": "assumption",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/157",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12000,
        "length": 68
      },
      "text": "Everyone who needs the app already has a corporate Entra ID account."
    },
    {
      "id": "a49",
      "type": "dependency",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/158",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12123,
        "length": 139
      },
      "text": "Before launch we need an export of the current catalogue and everyone's existing assessments out of Power Apps, from whoever owns that app."
    },
    {
      "id": "a50",
      "type": "dependency",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/159",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12447,
        "length": 149
      },
      "text": "At the start of the build we need an Entra ID app registration per environment, with redirect URIs and credentials, from the corporate identity team."
    },
    {
      "id": "a51",
      "type": "assumption",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/161",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12614,
        "length": 53
      },
      "text": "Telling people a write failed is our idea, not yours."
    },
    {
      "id": "a52",
      "type": "functional-requirement",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/161",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12668,
        "length": 152
      },
      "text": "Nobody asked for it, but with the Save button gone a failed write is otherwise invisible and the person walks away believing a false claim was recorded."
    },
    {
      "id": "a53",
      "type": "assumption",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/162",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12880,
        "length": 89
      },
      "text": "Should unrated and \"I have looked at this and it does not apply to me\" be the same thing?"
    },
    {
      "id": "a54",
      "type": "assumption",
      "elementId": "paragraphs/162",
      "span": {
        "offset": 12970,
        "length": 40
      },
      "text": "Today they are - a blank row means both."
    }
  ],
